@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `homecare-nouns`

-- Liberty HomeCare (UW-RPP-W-001-06-V): named cases and builders for the tests. No rules and
-- no assertions.
--
-- EVERY FIGURE HERE THAT THE DOCUMENT LEAVES TO THE POLICY SUMMARY IS HYPOTHETICAL: the sums
-- insured, the limits, the Deductibles, the premium and the dates were chosen to make the
-- arithmetic visible. The document states none of them. Figures the document does state
-- (40,000,000; 5%; 10%; 160,000,000; 50%; 4,000,000; 72 hours; 30 days; 12 months; the
-- short-period scale) are never typed here; the tests read them from the rules.

§ `Fixtures`

§§ `A policy`

-- A Summary for the year 2026: the Home insured for 2,000,000,000, the Contents for
-- 500,000,000, no Renovation Costs; Part 2 limits of 1,000,000,000 per Occurrence and
-- 2,000,000,000 for the Period, 100,000,000 for food and drink; Deductibles 2,000,000 under
-- Part 1 and 1,000,000 under Part 2, none under Part 3. All hypothetical.
GIVETH A `The Policy Summary`
`the 2026 Summary` MEANS
    `The Policy Summary` WITH
        `the Period of Insurance begins`                         IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `the Period of Insurance ends`                           IS YMD 2026 12 31
        `the sum insured on the Home`                            IS JUST 2_000_000_000
        `the sum insured on the Renovation Costs`                IS NOTHING
        `the sum insured on the Contents`                        IS JUST 500_000_000
        `the Part 1 Limit of Liability`                          IS NOTHING
        `the Part 2 Limit of Liability for any one Occurrence`   IS JUST 1_000_000_000
        `the Part 2 Limit of Liability for the Period`           IS JUST 2_000_000_000
        `the Part 2 limit for food and drink`                    IS JUST 100_000_000
        `the Part 1 Deductible`                                  IS JUST 2_000_000
        `the Part 2 Deductible`                                  IS JUST 1_000_000
        `the Part 3 Deductible`                                  IS NOTHING
        `the Insured is named under Part 3`                      IS TRUE
        `the domestic helper benefit is named`                   IS TRUE
        `the construction of the Home is specially provided for` IS FALSE
        `the annual premium`                                     IS 4_000_000

-- The same, for a tenant: Renovation Costs and Contents insured, the Home not.
GIVETH A `The Policy Summary`
`the 2026 tenant's Summary` MEANS
    `The Policy Summary` WITH
        `the Period of Insurance begins`                         IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `the Period of Insurance ends`                           IS YMD 2026 12 31
        `the sum insured on the Home`                            IS NOTHING
        `the sum insured on the Renovation Costs`                IS JUST 200_000_000
        `the sum insured on the Contents`                        IS JUST 300_000_000
        `the Part 1 Limit of Liability`                          IS NOTHING
        `the Part 2 Limit of Liability for any one Occurrence`   IS JUST 1_000_000_000
        `the Part 2 Limit of Liability for the Period`           IS JUST 2_000_000_000
        `the Part 2 limit for food and drink`                    IS JUST 100_000_000
        `the Part 1 Deductible`                                  IS JUST 2_000_000
        `the Part 2 Deductible`                                  IS NOTHING
        `the Part 3 Deductible`                                  IS NOTHING
        `the Insured is named under Part 3`                      IS TRUE
        `the domestic helper benefit is named`                   IS FALSE
        `the construction of the Home is specially provided for` IS FALSE
        `the annual premium`                                     IS 3_000_000

GIVEN kind IS A `A kind of building`
GIVETH A `The insured premises`
`premises that are a` kind MEANS
    `The insured premises` WITH
        `the kind of building`                                     IS kind
        `at the address in the Policy Summary`                     IS TRUE
        `the Insured's principal personal residence`               IS TRUE
        `used wholly or mainly as the Insured's private residence` IS TRUE
        `part used as an office`                                   IS FALSE
        `office use approved by the authorities`                   IS FALSE
        `used for a trade or business other than an office`        IS FALSE
        `walls of concrete, brick or stone`                        IS TRUE
        `roof of concrete, tiles, slate or incombustible metal sheet` IS TRUE
        `under construction`                                       IS FALSE
        `being demolished or vacant pending demolition`            IS FALSE
        `a temporary building or structure`                        IS FALSE
        `enclosed by walls or fences`                              IS TRUE
        `some part is lent, let or sublet`                         IS FALSE
        `some part is used to manufacture, deposit or store goods` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `The insured premises`
`a brick house` MEANS `premises that are a` `a house`

GIVEN tenant IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The Insured person`
`an Insured born 15 June 1980, a tenant` tenant MEANS
    `The Insured person` WITH
        `date of birth`                                        IS YMD 1980 6 15
        `owns the Home or is legally responsible for its care` IS NOT tenant
        `a tenant of the Home`                                 IS tenant

GIVEN summary  IS A `The Policy Summary`
      insured  IS A `The Insured person`
      premises IS A `The insured premises`
GIVETH A `The policy`
`a policy with` summary `, insured` insured `, premises` premises MEANS
    `The policy` WITH
        `the Policy Summary`                                     IS summary
        `the Insured`                                            IS insured
        `the premises`                                           IS premises
        `issued to a company`                                    IS FALSE
        `the Insured also has Personal Accident cover`           IS FALSE
        `the Insurer agreed to issue a Certificate or the Policy Summary` IS TRUE
        `the Insurer received and accepted a completed Proposal Form`     IS TRUE
        `the premium was paid in full within the prescribed time`         IS TRUE
        `the premium paid`                                       IS 4_000_000

-- The owner-occupier's policy: a brick house, Home and Contents insured.
GIVETH A `The policy`
`the owner's policy` MEANS
    `a policy with` `the 2026 Summary` `, insured` (`an Insured born 15 June 1980, a tenant` FALSE) `, premises` `a brick house`

GIVEN premises IS A `The insured premises`
GIVETH A `The policy`
`the owner's policy, at` premises MEANS
    `a policy with` `the 2026 Summary` `, insured` (`an Insured born 15 June 1980, a tenant` FALSE) `, premises` premises

-- The tenant's policy: an apartment, Renovation Costs and Contents insured.
GIVETH A `The policy`
`the tenant's policy` MEANS
    `a policy with` `the 2026 tenant's Summary` `, insured` (`an Insured born 15 June 1980, a tenant` TRUE) `, premises` (`premises that are a` `an apartment in an apartment building`)

§§ `The Insured's conduct`

-- An Insured who did everything the policy asks, with the written claim delivered on
-- 20 March 2026 (ten days after the loss dates used below).
GIVEN `delivered on` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `The Insured's conduct`
`conduct with the written claim delivered` `delivered on` MEANS
    `The Insured's conduct` WITH
        `observed and fulfilled the terms of the policy`                 IS TRUE
        `the statements in the Proposal Form were true`                  IS TRUE
        `misrepresented, misdescribed or omitted a matter in a document` IS FALSE
        `the Insurer elected to avoid the policy for misdescription`     IS FALSE
        `the Insured Location was used other than as a residence`        IS FALSE
        `precautions or circumstances changed so as to increase the risk` IS FALSE
        `the property was moved to another building or place`            IS FALSE
        `consecutive days the Home had been vacant`                      IS 0
        `the interest passed otherwise than by will or operation of law` IS FALSE
        `the Insurer endorsed its consent before the loss`               IS FALSE
        `gave immediate written notice with full particulars`            IS TRUE
        `forwarded every writ, summons and notice on receipt`            IS TRUE
        `admitted or offered payment without written consent`            IS FALSE
        `notified the police immediately`                                IS TRUE
        `acted immediately to minimise the loss`                         IS TRUE
        `disclosed all other insurances`                                 IS TRUE
        `the date the written claim was delivered`                       IS `delivered on`
        `the date to which the Insurer extended time in writing`         IS NOTHING
        `kept receipts or proof of value`                                IS TRUE
        `took reasonable precautions`                                    IS TRUE
        `obstructed or failed to comply with the Insurer's requirements` IS FALSE
        `the claim is fraudulent in any respect`                         IS FALSE
        `used fraudulent means or devices`                               IS FALSE
        `the loss was caused wilfully or with the Insured's connivance`  IS FALSE
        `the date the claim was rejected`                                IS NOTHING
        `the date the rejection was challenged`                          IS NOTHING
        `the date of an arbitral award on the claim`                     IS NOTHING
        `the date the award was challenged`                              IS NOTHING

GIVETH A `The Insured's conduct`
`good conduct` MEANS `conduct with the written claim delivered` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 20))

-- The day the questions are asked, unless a test says otherwise.
GIVETH A DATE
`1 April 2026` MEANS YMD 2026 4 1

§§ `Losses under Part 1`

-- A loss on 10 March 2026, inside a lockable part of the Home, owned by the Insured,
-- damaged (not destroyed), sudden and unforeseen, the Home attended throughout.
GIVEN item          IS A `A Part 1 item`
      property      IS A LIST OF `A description of property`
      cause         IS A `A cause of loss`
      circumstances IS A LIST OF `A circumstance of a loss`
GIVETH A `A Part 1 loss`
`a loss to` item `of` property `by` cause `with` circumstances MEANS
    `a loss to` item `of` property `owned by` `the Insured` `at` `inside a lockable part of the Home`
        `on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `by` cause `with` circumstances `, unattended for` 0 `days`

GIVEN item          IS A `A Part 1 item`
      property      IS A LIST OF `A description of property`
      owner         IS AN `An owner of property`
      place         IS A `A place where property was`
      date          IS A DATE
      cause         IS A `A cause of loss`
      circumstances IS A LIST OF `A circumstance of a loss`
      unattended    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A Part 1 loss`
`a loss to` item `of` property `owned by` owner `at` place `on` date `by` cause `with` circumstances `, unattended for` unattended `days` MEANS
    `A Part 1 loss` WITH
        `the item claimed`                                   IS item
        `the property`                                       IS property
        `whose property`                                     IS owner
        `where the property was`                             IS place
        `the date of the loss`                               IS date
        `the cause`                                          IS cause
        `the circumstances`                                  IS circumstances
        `the extent`                                         IS `damaged`
        `sudden and unforeseen`                              IS TRUE
        `consecutive days the Home had been left unattended` IS unattended

-- The house itself, damaged.
GIVEN cause         IS A `A cause of loss`
      circumstances IS A LIST OF `A circumstance of a loss`
GIVETH A `A Part 1 loss`
`the house damaged by` cause `with` circumstances MEANS
    `a loss to` `the Home` `of` (LIST `the house or apartment itself`) `by` cause `with` circumstances

-- A sofa, as Contents.
GIVEN cause         IS A `A cause of loss`
      circumstances IS A LIST OF `A circumstance of a loss`
GIVETH A `A Part 1 loss`
`a sofa damaged by` cause `with` circumstances MEANS
    `a loss to` `the Contents` `of` (LIST `furniture, a refrigerator, washing machine or similar household good`) `by` cause `with` circumstances

§§ `Settlement figures`

-- The adjuster's figures for a Part 1 loss.
GIVEN cost        IS A NUMBER
      `actual`    IS A NUMBER
      `reinstated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `whole`     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `The figures for a Part 1 loss`
`figures: reinstatement` cost `, Actual Value` `actual` `, reinstated and incurred` `reinstated` `, cost if wholly lost` `whole` MEANS
    `The figures for a Part 1 loss` WITH
        `the cost of reinstatement`                                      IS cost
        `the Actual Value`                                               IS `actual`
        `reinstatement was begun and carried out with reasonable dispatch` IS `reinstated`
        `the cost of reinstatement has actually been incurred`           IS `reinstated`
        `the cost of reinstatement had the property been wholly lost`    IS `whole`
        `the cost had reinstatement been lawfully possible`              IS NOTHING
        `the pair or set`                                                IS NOTHING
        `the amount already paid on this item in the Period`             IS 0
        `the Insurer agreed to reinstate the sum insured`                IS FALSE
        `the sums insured by other insurances of the same loss`          IS EMPTY

-- No Extension costs, and a claim of the given amount.
GIVEN claimed IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The costs claimed under the Part 1 Extensions`
`no Extension costs on a claim of` claimed MEANS
    `The costs claimed under the Part 1 Extensions` WITH
        `the claim for this loss`                                   IS claimed
        `architects', surveyors' and engineers' fees incurred`      IS 0
        `the fees allowed by the scales of the professional bodies` IS 0
        `fire fighting costs incurred`                              IS 0
        `costs of removing debris`                                  IS 0
        `costs of dismantling or demolishing`                       IS 0
        `costs of shoring or propping up`                           IS 0
        `costs of temporary protection`                             IS 0

§§ `Claims under Part 2`

-- A visitor, not related, who has not lived at the Home.
GIVETH A `A person injured`
`a visitor` MEANS
    `A person injured` WITH
        `relation to the Insured`                                           IS NOTHING
        `regularly lives with the Insured at the Insured Location`          IS FALSE
        `has used the Home`                                                 IS TRUE
        `has used the Home as a place to live`                              IS FALSE
        `lives with the Insured`                                            IS FALSE
        `days the person intends or intended to make the Home the main residence` IS 0
        `consecutive days the person used the Home or lived with the Insured` IS 0
        `employed by the Insured or a resident and injured in that work`    IS FALSE

-- A Part 2 claim on 10 March 2026: the named Insured held liable at the Insured Location,
-- connected with the Home, by first-instance judgment.
GIVEN person        IS A `A person held liable`
      harm          IS A LIST OF `A kind of harm`
      injured       IS A MAYBE `A person injured`
      damaged       IS A MAYBE `A third party's property`
      circumstances IS A LIST OF `A circumstance of a liability`
      forum         IS A `A forum`
GIVETH A `A Part 2 claim`
`a liability of` person `for` harm `to` injured `and` damaged `with` circumstances `, decided by` forum MEANS
    `A Part 2 claim` WITH
        `the person held liable`                          IS person
        `the date of the Occurrence`                      IS YMD 2026 3 10
        `at or near the Insured Location`                 IS TRUE
        `connected with the ownership or use of the Home` IS TRUE
        `unexpected and unintended by the Insured`        IS TRUE
        `legally liable`                                  IS TRUE
        `the harm`                                        IS harm
        `the person injured`                              IS injured
        `the property damaged`                            IS damaged
        `the circumstances`                               IS circumstances
        `the general circumstances`                       IS EMPTY
        `the forum`                                       IS forum

-- The named Insured's dog bites a visitor: bodily injury, no other circumstance.
GIVETH A `A Part 2 claim`
`a visitor bitten by the Insured's dog` MEANS
    `a liability of` `the Insured named in the Policy Summary` `for` (LIST `bodily injury, illness or disability`)
        `to` (JUST `a visitor`) `and` NOTHING `with` EMPTY `, decided by` `a first-instance judgment of a competent Vietnamese court`

GIVEN circumstances IS A LIST OF `A circumstance of a liability`
GIVETH A `A Part 2 claim`
`a visitor injured with` circumstances MEANS
    `a liability of` `the Insured named in the Policy Summary` `for` (LIST `bodily injury, illness or disability`)
        `to` (JUST `a visitor`) `and` NOTHING `with` circumstances `, decided by` `a first-instance judgment of a competent Vietnamese court`

GIVEN damages  IS A NUMBER
      recovered IS A NUMBER
      consented IS A NUMBER
      `paid before` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The figures for a Part 2 claim`
`Part 2 figures: damages` damages `, costs recovered` recovered `, consented costs` consented `, paid earlier` `paid before` MEANS
    `The figures for a Part 2 claim` WITH
        `the damages for which the Insured is liable`       IS damages
        `the claimant's costs recovered from the Insured`   IS recovered
        `costs incurred with the Insurer's written consent` IS consented
        `paid under Part 2 earlier in the Period`           IS `paid before`
        `paid for food and drink earlier in the Period`     IS 0
